cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "optcurves: consecutive convexity violations of gradient-descent optimization curves"
abstract: >-
  Performance-estimation study, exact rational certificates and counterexamples, and Lean-verified theorems on
  when the optimization curve of gradient descent with constant step size can be concave at several consecutive
  steps, for L-smooth convex and strongly convex functions. For one violation and mu-strongly convex functions,
  symbolic (SymPy-checked) proofs give the exact step-size threshold
  h_1(kappa) = (1 + kappa) - sqrt((1 + kappa)^2 - (7 kappa + 1)/2), kappa = L/mu, and the exact worst-case
  violation above it, h^2 max(0, -q) / (2 (2 + h^2 (1 - mu))) ||x_0 - x*||^2 with
  q = 2 mu h^2 - 4 (1 + mu) h + mu + 7.
type: software
